Jahmyr Gibbs and Bijan Robinson are splitting the top pick, but the Rams&#8217; Puka Nacua is the name climbing draft boards across campus leagues this month.

UCPD is investigating an alleged drug-facilitated aggravated assault that occurred on Gayley Avenue on Wednesday.&#160;
A UCLA student attended a party on the 600 block of Gayley Avenue – where UCLA’s fraternities are located – and saw someone add an unidentified powder to his drink before he was pressured to drink it, according to a Thursday UCPD Clery Timely Warning alert.&#160;
UCPD does not know the identity of the perpetrator and if they are affiliated with UCLA, said Richard Mejia, the director of emergency communications and information, in an email statement.&#160;
People with information related to the incident should contact UCPD, the alert stated.

SAN FRANCISCO – Before the goodbye, there must be a hello.&#160;
&#160;
Outside Lands 2026 kicked off with a highly anticipated set from Charli xcx, who debuted at the festival as a headliner.

Suki Waterhouse, an English singer-songwriter, actress and model performed on the Fairbanks Lawn at the Hollywood Forever Cemetery on July 23, marking the second stop of “The Loveland Tour.”&#160;
&#160;
Waterhouse released her third studio album, “Loveland,” on July 10 before kicking off the tour in Phoenix on July 22.&#160;
&#160;
Charlotte Lawrence and her band opened the show with a set that included a cover and an unreleased single.

UCPD arrested a man for indecent exposure near the Luskin School of Public Affairs building Wednesday.
The man was non-compliant with sex offender registration requirements, said Jeffrey Chobanian, the captain of UCPD’s operations bureau, in an emailed statement.&#160;
He added in the statement that the man had a felony arrest warrant with the California Department of Corrections and Rehabilitation for a weapons violation.
